DoProc with an unqualified target inside a class method
(diag.doproc_in_class, error): the compiler rejects it; Me:Method() is the
fix. Near misses in the same method: a fully qualified external target
(issue #151), a non-literal target, and ExecFunction (no class-method
restriction).
-- input.ssl --
:CLASS Validator;
:DECLARE aErrors;

:PROCEDURE Check;
	:PARAMETERS oInput, sRule;
	:DECLARE bOk, bShape, bCustom, vExt;
	bOk := DoProc("CheckRequired", {oInput});
	bShape := DoProc("Lab.ShapeRules.Validate", {oInput});
	bCustom := DoProc(sRule, {oInput});
	vExt := ExecFunction("Lab.ShapeRules", {oInput});
	:RETURN bOk .AND. bShape .AND. bCustom .AND. Me:CheckRequired(oInput);
:ENDPROC;

:PROCEDURE CheckRequired;
	:PARAMETERS oInput;
	:RETURN .NOT. Empty(oInput);
:ENDPROC;
-- format --
:CLASS Validator;
:DECLARE aErrors;

:PROCEDURE Check;
	:PARAMETERS oInput, sRule;
	:DECLARE bOk, bShape, bCustom, vExt;

	bOk := DoProc("CheckRequired", {oInput});
	bShape := DoProc("Lab.ShapeRules.Validate", {oInput});
	bCustom := DoProc(sRule, {oInput});
	vExt := ExecFunction("Lab.ShapeRules", {oInput});

	:RETURN bOk .AND. bShape .AND. bCustom .AND. Me:CheckRequired(oInput);
:ENDPROC;

:PROCEDURE CheckRequired;
	:PARAMETERS oInput;

	:RETURN .NOT. Empty(oInput);
:ENDPROC;
-- diagnostics --
7:9-7:15 error doproc_in_class: Unqualified DoProc targets are a compile-time error inside class methods. Use Me:MethodName() / Base:MethodName(), or a fully qualified "Category.Script.Procedure" reference for a deployed procedure.
-- diagnostics [--strict --info] --
7:9-7:15 error doproc_in_class: Unqualified DoProc targets are a compile-time error inside class methods. Use Me:MethodName() / Base:MethodName(), or a fully qualified "Category.Script.Procedure" reference for a deployed procedure.
